      "key": {
        "uuid": "a0f83917_82856e3c",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 506,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-16T17:49:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It won\u0027t trigger, just like WARN_ONs elsewhere in this file won\u0027t trigger (e.g. lines 475, 490, 535, and many more in the trusty_log_seq_* functions above). I can certainly leave this check out, but the coding convention in this file appears to be to defend against the impossible, so I did.",
      "parentUuid": "54c36522_299385ff",
      "revId": "a375da85873fb1afff209655445f14c04ed0f182",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92135a83_ba38bf3f",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 506,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-16T18:46:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Defending against bugs is fine. If the bug you are protecting against is that trusty_log_sfile_dev_open was not call, this check won\u0027t work though as the pointer does not start out as NULL.",
      "parentUuid": "a0f83917_82856e3c",
      "revId": "a375da85873fb1afff209655445f14c04ed0f182",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "69c1bf10_11cded65",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 506,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-16T20:02:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s defending against sfile being NULL, because sfile is dereferenced immediately below.\nOnce sfile has been determined to be non-NULL, it is assumed to be the pointer that dev_open put there.\n\nMaybe I\u0027m misunderstanding your objection, but this seems pretty much exactly the same to me as e.g. line 475, where we check that file-\u003eprivate_data is not NULL, and then assume that it points to the exact misc_device structure we used when registering the device. There are other examples above where we do the same: check that something is not NULL, and then assume that it is a pointer to the thing we expect.",
      "parentUuid": "92135a83_ba38bf3f",
      "revId": "a375da85873fb1afff209655445f14c04ed0f182",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a69d1308_184664f5",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 506,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-16T20:45:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, but at line 475 only one object type has been assigned to that variable. In this code you are relying on trusty_log_sfile_dev_open to have changed it from one type of object to another. I\u0027m not sure that this check does anything useful. I guess this will catch a bug where trusty_log_sfile_dev_poll gets called even if trusty_log_sfile_dev_open returned an error, as trusty_log_sfile_dev_poll leaved the pointer NULL in that case, but this seems to be the only bug that this guards against as the pointer starts out as something else. You could add a comment stating that if you want to, but I don\u0027t think this check is strictly needed as I assume that is not supposed to happen.",
      "parentUuid": "69c1bf10_11cded65",
      "revId": "a375da85873fb1afff209655445f14c04ed0f182",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "006c4097_621d481f",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 506,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-16T21:29:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, this is strictly to check for null before dereferencing the pointer, same as is (unnecessarily) done throughout this file.\n\nAs for dev_open changing what private_data points to, that\u0027s not even happening yet at line 475. Line 475 checks whether private_data is NULL, even though the API says that field will not be NULL. And then when it is not NULL, it assumes that it is the type it supposed to be. That\u0027s the exact same thing that\u0027s done here in dev_poll.\n\nI agree that this check isn\u0027t actually useful here, but neither are the majority of similar checks in this file. I want to be consistent. Either we should do the same check here, or we should remove the other checks too. I\u0027d be happy to do a separate cleanup pass after this to remove all the unnecessary checks.",
      "parentUuid": "a69d1308_184664f5",
      "revId": "a375da85873fb1afff209655445f14c04ed0f182",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
